{
  "schema": 1,
  "id": "elementary-metadata",
  "gate": "required",
  "operation": "elementary-metadata",
  "candidate": "codec-views-worker",
  "worker_operation": "elementary-metadata-",
  "contract": [
    "Force the same elementary format on both sides over a preloaded seekable source. Read the first packet carrying audio, skipping complete leading ID3 envelopes, then fold codec, sample rate, channels, declared duration in samples, and start trim in samples. For FLAC with STREAMINFO, compare its original bytes and read its source declarations independently of the reference demuxer’s first-packet context. AAC rate and channels and E-AC-3 channels are compared by the wire oracle.",
    "Check AAC and E-AC-3 track rates and channel counts against the first frame's original source bytes, using its physical offset and extent. Apply the ADTS coded channel configuration and the Enhanced AC-3 sampling and coding-mode fields, including the low-frequency channel bit.",
    "For MPEG audio, read through the footer in the candidate to include ID3v1 and APEv2 tags. Compare the sorted dictionary projection with the reference format dictionary. The projection includes the shared title, artist, album_artist, album, date, track, disc, composer, copyright, encoded_by, publisher, encoder and comment keys. Decode ID3v2 text frames by their encoding and ID3v1 fields as Latin-1. Compare the FLAC comment through the same key set. The FLAC display dictionary joins repeated values in source order with a semicolon.",
    "The separate wire comparison covers physical metadata and tag layout, SEEKTABLE points that lack a public reference index view, first frame headers, Xing/Info fields and the LAME view. The reference's skip-sample side data is a decoder trim and is compared to candidate packet trim."
  ],
  "required_profiles": [
    "aac",
    "ac3",
    "eac3",
    "flac",
    "mp3"
  ],
  "required_targets": [
    "aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu",
    "thumbv7neon-unknown-linux-gnueabihf"
  ],
  "iterations": 20,
  "minimum_pairs": 30,
  "confidence": 0.95,
  "runner": "cargo xtask report",
  "reference": "ffmpeg-codec-views-native",
